# Q9 -- MLIP run + trained model (Q11 compute-cost properties inline)
###############################################################################

# No training run or trained model is reported by the paper (see Q12).

###############################################################################
# Q10 -- Benchmark results
###############################################################################

# No energy/force/stress accuracy metric is reported in a form the schema captures (see Q12).

###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# About 14 million CPU core-hours were spent generating the data (a cost
# of the reference calculations, not of a potential).

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Data-descriptor paper: no MLIP method, run, model or benchmark result (Q7-Q10 empty). The potentials built on these data are in smith2018 (ANI-1x) and smith2019ccx (ANI-1ccx), whose data-set nodes are separate, paper-local nodes.
# - numConfigurations are the rounded figures of the abstract. mlips:DLPNO_CCSDT is used for the wave-function method of the composite scheme, as in smith2019ccx.
# - The def2-TZVPP subset and the additional properties (dipoles, quadrupoles, charges, volumes) are not modelled.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
